        <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/AISystem/f1b3a5fe276a> .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/27c3c9c44a10> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In the US, 18 U.S. Code § 2256 defines \"child pornography\" as \"any visual depiction, including any photograph, film, video, picture, or computer or computer-generated image or picture, whether made or produced by electronic, mechanical, or other means, of sexually explicit conduct.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3351" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4425fb2fc413> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google’s initial version of the Imagen text-to-image AI tool, released only for research, trained on a different variant of LAION’s datasets called LAION-400M, an older version of 5B." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3341" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4e35d7487b36> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to a new study by the Stanford Internet Observatory shared with 404 Media ahead of publication, the researchers found the suspected instances of CSAM through a combination of perceptual and cryptographic hash-based detection and analysis of the images themselves." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4fa74bb72ff7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In response to the findings, the organization decided to temporarily take down its datasets, including LAION-5B and another named LAION-400M." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3353" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a24975436e0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Publicly accessible generative AI models, like Stable Diffusion XL1.5 and MidJourney, have been documented to have been trained on datasets containing CSAM such as LAION-5B." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3351" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5a953172c916> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Stable Diffusion, one of the most popular text-to-image generative AI tools on the market from the $1 billion startup Stability AI, was trained on a trove of illegal child sexual abuse material, according to new research from the Stanford Internet Observatory." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3352" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5b75ab486a49> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "LAION confirmed the presence of child sexual abuse material (CSAM) in the dataset, called LAION-5B, and scrubbed it from their online channels." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/64edab22c890> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3875] The alleged distribution of child sexual abuse images on the messaging app Telegram is part of what led French authorities to bring charges on Wednesday against the platform's founder and CEO, Pavel Durov." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3875" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6b6f63fbfff3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As VentureBeat reported in September, Andrew Ng, former co-founder and head of Google Brain, has made no bones about the fact that the latest advances in machine learning have depended on free access to large quantities of data, much of it scraped from the open internet." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6dc5dca2d144> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3343] A widely-used artificial intelligence data set used to train Stable Diffusion, Imagen and other AI image generator models has been removed by its creator after a study found it contained thousands of instances of suspected child sexual abuse material." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3343" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6efc138915fd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "That being said, the LAION-5B is a renowned open dataset that is best known for being the tool used by Stable Diffusion 1.5, with the investigation claiming that these models were trained directly on CSAM." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3355" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a119fc88f8cd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The dataset underpins widely used models such as Stable Diffusion 1.5 and Midjourney and was found to contain no less than 1,679 instances of CSAM." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3351" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a286e99770ee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to an April 2023 Bloomberg article, Schuhmann was hanging out on a Discord server for AI enthusiasts and was inspired by the first iteration of OpenAI's DALL-E to make sure there would be an open-source dataset to help train image-to-text diffusion models." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cee6a3806911> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Our new investigation reveals that these models are trained directly on CSAM present in a public dataset of billions of images, known as LAION-5B." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3324" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d4f911f74606> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "400-M was also removed by LAION, out of an \"abundance of caution\" concerning the findings of the paper." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d8fbf182489d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Stable Diffusion, one of the most commonly used text-to-image generation systems, is based on LAION data, for example." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dc22da6229d4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "LAION-5B, a dataset used by Stable Diffusion creator Stability AI, included at least 1,679 illegal images scraped from social media posts and popular adult websites." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3341" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e0ac18960de2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3343] A Dec. 20 report from researchers at the Stanford Internet Observatory's Cyber Policy Center said they identified 3,226 instances of suspected CSAM --- or child sexual abuse material --- in the LAION-5B data set, 'much of which was confirmed as CSAM by third parties,' according to Stanford Cyber Policy Center's Big Data Architect and Chief Technologist David Thiel." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3343" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f89fe6a69c0e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Furthermore, the PROTECT Act of 2003 outlaws any \"drawing, cartoon, sculpture, or painting\" that \"depicts a minor [or someone appearing to be a minor] engaging in sexually explicit conduct.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3351" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e1f8f03a653> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The first research version of Google's Imagen text-to-image model was trained on LAION-400M, but that was never released; Google says that none of the following iterations of Imagen use any LAION datasets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3354" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0c23a1382c86> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"Removal of the identified source material is currently in progress as researchers reported the image URLs to the National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC) in the US and the C3P,\" the SIO said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1044b86d1f10> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Also last December, researchers at the social media analytics firm Graphika found a proliferation of dozens of \"undressing\" services, many based on open-source AI image generators, likely including Stable Diffusion." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/13f561f912e0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "To find images in the dataset worth testing, SIO focused on images tagged by LAION's safety classifier as \"unsafe.\" Those images were scanned with PhotoDNA to detect CSAM, and matches were sent to the Canadian Centre for Child Protection (C3P) to be verified." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/149c83932567> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "last October, a report from the U.K. nonprofit Internet Watch Foundation (which collects reports of child sexual abuse material) detailed the ease with which malicious actors are now making photorealistic AI-generated child sexual abuse material, at scale." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/19d1ae6aefcd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We asked Stability AI, which funds and steers the development of Stable Diffusion, if it knew about the presence of CSAM in LAION-5B, and if any of that material made its way into the startup's series of models; the company didn't respond to our questions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1cc18ed66153> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Following Champandard's tweets, Hugging Face's chief ethics scientist Margaret Mitchell wrote on Mastodon: \"I just wanted to pop in to say that there has been a lot of time and energy spent on trying to find CSAM, and none has been found." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1d9499accc79> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "LAION-5B was submitted to the highly influential Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS) conference for peer review, where it was accepted and awarded the best paper in the \"datasets and benchmarks\" track." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3351" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1db8565d6b72> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Despite LAION's attempts to classify whether the content was sexually explicit or whether data contained underage explicit content, models were trained on a wide array of benign and graphic content." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/270362de7eea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A previous SIO report with the nonprofit online child safety group Thorn found rapid advances in generative machine learning make it possible to create realistic imagery that facilitates child sexual exploitation using open source AI image generation models." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3324" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e71be038e9a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Midjourney, the research lab behind another prominent AI image generator, also uses LAION-5B." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3352" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/394e6049ce2f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hamburg, Germany-based high school teacher and trained actor Christoph Schuhmann helped found LAION, short for \"Large-scale AI Open Network." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/39c8a8960435> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Thiel told me he continued to pursue the topic after a tip from AI researcher Alex Champandard, who found a URL of an image in LAION-5B on Hugging Face that was captioned with a phrase in Spanish that appeared to describe child exploitation material." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/40dbadfa1b7d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The dataset was created by LAION, a non-profit organization behind the massive image datasets used by generative AI systems like Stable Diffusion." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/414290ab413b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's worth noting that Jeff Allen, a data scientist at the Integrity Institute, found that Stable Diffusion 1.5 was downloaded from Hugging Face over 6 million times in the past month, making it the most popular AI image-generator on the platform." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4e0e331733db> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But a report last year by the Stanford Internet Observatory found it contained links to sexually explicit images of children, contributing to the ease with which some AI tools have been able to produce photorealistic deepfakes that depict children." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3875" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51806cdbb095> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We collaborate with universities, researchers and NGOs to improve these filters and are currently working with the Internet Watch Foundation (IWF) to identify and remove content suspected of violating laws." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6785dfe77e50> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Following publication of the paper, a Google spokesperson told 404 Media: \"Imagen has never used LAION-5B." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6af60394567e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "LAION lead engineer Richard Vencu wrote in response to a researcher asking how LAION handles potential illegal data that might be included in the dataset." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e2b8a35b1cc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "AI pioneer Andrew Ng has criticized removing access to LAION" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7e440435839a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sasha Luccioni, an AI and data ethics researcher at HuggingFace who co-authored the paper with Birhane, told Motherboard." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3350" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/84958efaa56f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to their paper, they employed \"perceptual hash‐based detection, cryptographic hash‐based detection, and nearest‐neighbors analysis leveraging the image embeddings in the dataset itself.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3354" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a32e35c2a21c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In September 2022, there was an instance of an artist discovering private medical record photos taken by her doctor in 2013 referenced in the LAION-5B image dataset. The artist, Lapine, discovered the photos on the Have I Been Trained website, which allows people to look for their work in popular AI training datasets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aeb31bb091f5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "David Thiel, lead author of the study and Chief Technologist at the Stanford Internet Observatory told 404 Media." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/afb614de7eff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "LAION-5B is available for download from Hugging Face as an open-source tool." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bb2f4695f4af> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "While some companies are trying to improve their products' safety with the help of the Tech Coalition, what progress have we seen on the broader issue?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d4516dfbc405> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Gizmodo reached out to Stability AI for comment and will update this story if it responds." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3347" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d83e00fb84e1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"That was a surprise because no one had looked at that before,\" Jesse Dodge, a research scientist at the Allen Institute for AI, told VentureBeat in November." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d8c65c3ded35> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hannah Wong, a spokesperson for OpenAI---creator of Stable Diffusion rival DALL-E---said OpenAI does not train on any LAION dataset, including 5B." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3352" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e182ce7047f4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "While it's the first time German non-profit LAION's AI training data has been accused of harboring child porn, the organization has caught flack for including questionable content in its training data before." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e58f539e0dd2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "LAION's 5B data set has since been taken offline, and the non-profit is working closely with the Internet Watch Foundation, a charity dedicated to protecting children worldwide by removing and preventing abusive content online." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/39d35422aac5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In an issue of his DeepLearning.ai newsletter, The Batch, titled \"It's Time to Update Copyright for Generative AI\", he wrote that a lack of access to massive popular datasets such as Common Crawl, The Pile, and LAION would put the brakes on progress or at least radically alter the economics of current research." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/50782ee824a4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Researchers at Stanford's Internet Observatory and the technology non-profit Thorn published a troubling report in June 2023." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6bb34134cafc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The LAION research dataset is a huge index of online images and captions that's been a source for leading AI image-makers such as Stable Diffusion and Midjourney." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3875" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/707f1e3795ea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "To sift through this expansive data tranche, researchers used PhotoDNA, a proprietary content filtering tool developed by Microsoft to help organizations identify and report certain types of prohibited content, including CSAM." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3347" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d4a716626b93> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A massive open-source AI dataset, LAION-5B, which has been used to train popular AI text-to-image generators like Stable Diffusion 1.5 and Google's Imagen, contains at least 1,008 instances of child sexual abuse material, a new report from the Stanford Internet Observatory found --- with thousands more instances suspected." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e3463a8044a4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "LAION told 404 Media on Tuesday that out of \"an abundance of caution,\" it was taking down its datasets, including LAION-5B and another called LAION-400M temporarily \"to ensure they are safe before republishing them.\"",
        "LAION told 404 Media on Tuesday that out of \"an abundance of caution,\" it was taking down its datasets..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4c5d36601681> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Hash matches indicate definite, known CSAM, and were sent to the Project Arachnid Shield API and validated by Canadian Centre for Child Protection, which is able to view, verify, and report those images to the authorities." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7b31ef133aa5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 of the LAION-based tools that Stanford identified as the \"most popular model for generating explicit imagery\" --- an older and lightly filtered version of Stable Diffusion --- remained easily accessible until Thursday, when the New York-based company Runway ML removed it from the AI model repository Hugging Face." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3875" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/da43425933e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Stanford Internet Observatory (SIO) investigation identified hundreds of known images of child sexual abuse material (CSAM) in an open dataset used to train popular AI text-to-image generation models, such as Stable Diffusion.",
        "A Stanford Internet Observatory (SIO) investigation identified hundreds of known images of child sexual abuse material (CSAM) in an open dataset used to train popular AI text-to-image generation models." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3324" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e4272f48dfb0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "San Francisco's city attorney earlier this month filed a lawsuit seeking to shut down a group of websites that enable the creation of AI-generated nudes of women and girls." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3875" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe2e5084bc57> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Stanford researcher David Thiel, author of the December report, commended LAION for significant improvements but said the next step is to withdraw from distribution the \"tainted models\" that are still able to produce child abuse imagery." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3875" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/00014314e01e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In April, Thorn and All Tech Is Human announced an initiative to bring together mainstream tech companies, generative AI developers, model hosting platforms, and more to define and commit to Safety by Design principles, which put preventing child sexual abuse at the center of the product development process.",
        "In April, Thorn and All Tech Is Human announced an initiative to bring together mainstream tech companies, generative AI developers, model hosting platforms, and more to define and commit to Safety by Design principles." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0dc9154b5f38> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a study published today, the Stanford Internet Observatory (SIO) said it pored over more than 32 million data points in the LAION-5B dataset and was able to validate, using the Microsoft-developed tool PhotoDNA, 1,008 CSAM images -- some included multiple times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/52baa396689f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An image generator called Stable Diffusion version 1.5, which was created by the AI company Runway with funding from Stability AI, has been particularly implicated in the production of CSAM." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/89bb8618cbf8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We note that though Stability has released various spins of Stable Diffusion, including version 2.0 with the aforementioned filters, version 1.5, which was studied by the SIO and trained on LAION-5B, was released by another startup called RunwayML, which collaborates with Stability AI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9536cb6e23b7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A spokesperson for Stable Diffusion told 404 Media following publication of the paper: \"Stable Diffusion 1.5 was released by RunwayML, not Stability AI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3346" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b5b27ffbcaee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a recent paper from the Allen Institute for AI called \"What's in My Big Data?\", researchers studied LAION-2B-en, a subset of LAION-5B, which is 2.32 billion photo captions in English." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3349" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c8546855de2a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Stable Diffusion 1.5 was released by RunwayML, not Stability AI, he said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3352" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce7ee6b6074c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Stanford Internet Observatory revealed thousands of images of child sexual abuse in the LAION-5B data set, which supports many different AI models." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3348" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e4fba0e89c5c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After significant disputes, different companies have taken it upon themselves to make AI models safe, with OpenAI also announcing their new \"Preparedness Framework\" for it." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3355" .

