<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/AIModel/c8d4c81cd9a3> a airo:AIModel ;
    rdfs:label "OpenAI DALL-E" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.95"^^xsd:float ;
    airo:extractionMode "explicit" ;
    airo:hasDescription "DALL-E" ;
    airo:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a286e99770ee> ;
    airo:hasSourceDocument <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/document/3349> .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b778a40c10e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A new report from the Stanford Internet Observatory (SIO) and its researcher David Thiel uncovered an alarming case of AI training data that contained more than 1,000 child sexual abuse materials (CSAM)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3355" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2fd08845387f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Removal of the identified source material is currently in progress as researchers reported the image URLs to the National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC) in the U.S. and the Canadian Centre for Child Protection (C3P)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3324" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51ab81d87fa0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "US attorneys general have called on Congress to set up a committee to investigate the impact of AI on child exploitation and prohibit the creation of AI-generated CSAM." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3341" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/86db1661e229> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It's also collaborating with standard-setting institutions such as IEEE and NIST to integrate their efforts into new and existing standards, opening the door to third party audits that would \"move past the honor system,\" Portnoff says." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8c04e897cab7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "popular platforms such as Hugging Face and Civitai have been hosting that model and others that may have been trained on real images of child sexual abuse." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3874" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8cba265fde56> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google, which used a LAION-2B predecessor known as LAION-400M to train its Imagen AI generator, decided to never release the tool due to several concerns, including whether the LAION training data had helped it build a biased and problematic model." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3345" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a3cd60f15b89> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Durov's arrest \"signals a really big change in the whole tech industry that the founders of these platforms can be held personally responsible,\" said David Evan Harris, a researcher at the University of California, Berkeley who recently reached out to Runway asking about why the problematic AI image-generator was still publicly accessible." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3875" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d76d6c87e6b5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "These models are trained on datasets curated by scraping a massive amount of imagery and related text from the Internet---with different models from different firms like OpenAI or Stability AI using data collected through different sources." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3351" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d99147c612eb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Worried that the technology has outpaced federal laws protecting against child sexual abuse and the mining of their data, attorneys general across the U.S. recently called on Congress to take action to address the threat of AI CSAM." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3352" .

